      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "COMMANCHE JACK (1) is a sprinter who thrives over these shorter races. Was a winner last time (24.45) over 425m at Bendigo in a Grade 5 and is even better suited coming back in trip. Strike rate this course and distance strong having won four of eight tries. Form from his last run is proving to be solid. Can make it two on the bounce. FLAMING FOX (2) was strongly fancied latest and proved too good with a 3.5 lengths win at this track in a handy 19.38. Draws to advantage and goes well over this trip. Makes plenty of appeal on the back of that last-start win. SLICK TOMMY (8) placed three back at Geelong then out of the placings last couple but moves to box 8 this time where he has performed well. Can turn it around this time. PAW WALDO (6) with some luck can improve on an unplaced run last time here.",
